Cell["The scalar momenta p1 and p2 are incoming. FeynArts uses one outgoing graviton with momentum p1 + p2; its incoming momentum is therefore k = −p1 − p2. The loop momentum is l and the free graviton indices are μ and ν. Keep D, m and κ symbolic and use GaugeFixingEpsilon = 2. CreateFeynAmp uses PreFactor -> 1 and FCFAConvert uses Prefactor -> 1: retain the rule factors of i and native symmetry factors, without adding FeynArts’ default loop measure or its extra overall −i.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3498190c-a401-4efc-bf4a-45c330f2a939"],

Cell["\<\
The metric signature is (+, \[Minus], \[Minus], \[Minus]). The reported \
vertex is the amputated sum of the displayed Feynman-rule products, with \
their factors of i retained; it is not a separately normalized scattering \
matrix element.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13e86504-902a-461c-b7d0-84ae6c954b73"],

Cell["\<\
TID uses the FeynCalc convention in which a scalar loop integral becomes i \
\[Pi]\.b2 times its PaVe function. PaXImplicitPrefactor has its default value \
1: no factor (2\[Pi])^(\[Minus]D) is included here. The Package-X interface \
expands at D = 4 \[Minus] 2\[CurlyEpsilon]; EpsilonUV and EpsilonIR label the \
separated poles in that convention. These normalisations must be accounted \
for before comparing with a loop measure d^D l/(2\[Pi])^D.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18d1ae49-28df-4fb5-ac52-4f96d5e7379d"],

Cell["Use the existing scalar model with an arbitrary mass. Replace the potential couplings after conversion, leaving the model parameters unassigned. Excluding its six potential field points also prevents drawing diagrams that would vanish under these replacements. The minimal scalar–graviton couplings remain present.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cfc00c02-3386-44ae-aa33-8b850a7cd465"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"model", "=", "\"\<Single-Scalar-Tensor-Minimal-Coupling\>\""}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"InitializeModel", "[", 
   RowBox[{"model", ",", 
    RowBox[{"GenericModel", "\[Rule]", "model"}]}], "]"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"scalarParameters", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ScalarMass", "\[Rule]", "m"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"ScalarLambda3", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"ScalarLambda4", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"potentialVertices", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FieldPoint", "[", "0", "]"}], "@@", 
        RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"T", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", "h"}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"S", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", "n"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"h", ",", "0", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "1"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001727459604403*^9, 4.001727463563777*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"42cbb455-ee10-4dfb-8fed-a8934d6b6c39"],

